description: The door into this repository

! TW5-Syntax

A TextMate grammar for TiddlyWiki wikitext and the memetic dialect, and the instruments that hold
it to the parser it answers to.

!! What this wiki holds

|!Kind |!What it answers |!How it stays true |
|''judgement'' |a question no registry answers, which a person weighs |argued here, gated against what the host documents |
|''harvest'' |what the installed TiddlyWiki knows |written by a boot, never by a hand |

The two look alike — both JSON data tiddlers — and they fail differently. A judgement goes stale
when the world moves and nobody notices. A harvest goes stale on a version, and says so.

|!Tiddler |!Kind |
|<<lar-link "$:/tw5-syntax/BuiltInVariables">> |judgement — which names TiddlyWiki's core owns |
|<<lar-link "$:/tw5-syntax/ReaderRelations">> |judgement — what a reader must meet as one, and what a reader must tell apart |
|<<lar-link "$:/tw5-syntax/PlainConstructs">> |judgement — why a construct reads as prose rather than as a thing |
|<<lar-link "$:/tw5-syntax/GrammarSignals">> |harvest — every filter operator, widget and wikitext rule this TiddlyWiki registers |
|<<lar-link "$:/tw5-syntax/GateReport">> |harvest — what every gate said when it last ran |

Each judgement carries its own reason beside it. A reason belongs with the ruling it explains, and
a comment in a tool keeps it where nobody weighs it — so the wiki shows both, and a reason that
stops answering to anything fails the gate that reads it, the same way a missing ruling does.

!! Running a gate from here

The wiki that shows a ruling runs the instrument that enforces it:

```
tiddlywiki editions/tw5-syntax --gate list
tiddlywiki editions/tw5-syntax --gate colour-witness dark-construct
tiddlywiki editions/tw5-syntax --gate
```

The command stands in this wiki as <<lar-link "$:/tw5-syntax/modules/grammar-commands">>, so a
reader who wants to know what it does opens it rather than a file beside the wiki. Its gate list
comes from the manifest by way of the report, so one added joins without anybody remembering.

!! How a new TiddlyWiki reaches the grammar

# `npm run signals` boots this edition against the TiddlyWiki the repo answers to, and writes what it found.
# `npm run rule-coverage` holds the grammar to it: every wikitext rule the host stands, the grammar reads — under its own name, or under one a line declares.
# `npm run builtins -- --check` holds the grammar to the judgement beside it.
# A rule the host added and the grammar never learned fails the second step, so a version bump arrives as a failing gate rather than as a construct that quietly reads as prose.

Nothing in that chain edits the grammar for you. It reports what a release changed and stops, so
an operator decides what the change means.

!! Where the rest stands

|!Surface |!What it carries |
